msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What is the use of the bar above the programming part that gives the channel "
"name and channel freq ? it is exactly the same than in the listview?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The recorder, the player and the channellist are independent objects. The "
"recorder and the player have no access to the channellist. The bar reflects "
"the selection and is filled via signals and slots in kalva_viewer. It "
"provides these information to the recorder / player."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the movie tag, you have this calendar view. Why having the quit and "
"configure button there? Wouldn't it be better to  create a toolbar?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These Icons in the toolbar have nothing to do with the calender. As the "
"calender brings everything with it that it needs, I don't see any useful "
"actions for the toolbar that deal with the active tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:556
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The quit button shouldn't be there according to some HIGs. That is my "
"stubborness, I miss this feature that was eliminated from so many kde apps..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The other is there because one has to open the prefs for changing profiles. "
"As Kalva can provide many profiles for different purposes (16/9, 4/3, 50Hz "
"non interlaced for sport broadcasts...), I want the prefs window to be close "
"at hand."
msgstr ""

