msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to obtain &kalva;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:609
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You find &kalva; Sourcetarball and SuSE-RPMs at <ulink url=\"http://"
"developer.berlios.de/projects/kalva\">the &kalva; project site</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:615
#, no-c-format
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"MPlayer of course. The MPlayer package includes the MEcoder, which is the "
"working horse of &kalva;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:619
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"date is used to put the day and time of the recording into the filename for "
"the video."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid "at is used to schedule movie recordings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid "cron is used to schedule serial recordings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid "perl is needed for perl-setup-crontab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid "perl-setup-crontab is the interface of &kalva; to your crontab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:629
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"aumix is optional. It can be used to switch the audio channel to recording, "
"mute it when recording and raise the input gain. Beware that aumix does not "
"support all mixer channels. It might be that your tv card uses a channel "
"aumix can not set (like mine, my tv card is on video)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You also need at least the kde libraries if you want to use &kalva;. &kalva; "
"needs &kde; 3.x. Recommended is at least &kde; 3.4.0."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:634
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalva; itself can be downloaded as binary RPM (SuSE) or sourcetarball from "
"<ulink url=\"http://developer.berlios.de/projects/kalva\">the &kalva; "
"project site</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A list of frequent changes is available at <ulink url=\"http://kalva.berlios."
"de/#vlast\">http://kalva.berlios.de/#vlast</ulink>."
msgstr ""

